[b]Catch, battle, train and ride Pokémon in Minecraft Bedrock Edition.[/b] Pick a starter from any region, fill your Pokédex, build a team of six, take on Kanto's eight gym leaders, then climb the League tower to face the Elite Four and the Champion.

This is a Bedrock Edition add-on port of [b]Cobblemon[/b], the open-source Pokémon mod for Java Edition by the Cobblemon team. The Pokémon models, animations, textures, sounds and data all come from Cobblemon itself, converted by a script, so every Pokémon looks, moves and sounds the way it does in the mod.

[h2]Installation[/h2]
[list]
[*]Download [url=https://github.com/kirbycope/cobblemon-bedrock/releases/latest/download/cobblemon-bedrock.mcaddon]cobblemon-bedrock.mcaddon[/url] from the latest release.
[*]Double-click the .mcaddon file to import both packs into Minecraft Bedrock.
[*]In a world's settings, add the [b]Cobblemon[/b] behavior pack (it brings its resource pack with it) and load the world.
[/list]
No experiments are needed. Made for Minecraft Bedrock 1.26.52 and tested on a dedicated server.

[h2]How it works[/h2]
When you first join, the starter screen opens: choose a region, then your partner Pokémon. You also get two books, a [b]README[/b] with every control and a [b]Getting Started[/b] guide, and the [b]Party[/b] item. Your Pokémon travel with you in their Poké Balls and show down the left of your screen. Send one out with the Party item, battle wild Pokémon to level up, catch more with Poké Balls crafted from apricorns, and keep the rest in a PC. When your team is ready, go find a gym.

[h2]Gyms and the Kanto League[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]8 gyms[/b] generate in the world, each in the biome that suits it: Brock's Pewter Gym in the mountains, Misty's Cerulean Gym on beaches and in swamps, Lt. Surge's Vermilion Gym in badlands and savannas, Erika's Celadon Gym in flower and birch forests, Sabrina's Saffron Gym in dark forests and cherry groves, Koga's Fuchsia Gym in jungles, Blaine's Cinnabar Gym in the Nether, and Clair's Blackthorn Gym in the End.
[*][b]The Kanto League[/b] towers over the End islands, with the Elite Four (Lorelei, Bruno, Agatha and Lance) on its floors and Champion Terry at the top.
[*]Step on the plate in a gym's doorway and its leader appears. Talk to them to battle. Every leader has a full team with set moves, abilities and held items, uses potions, and picks its moves to win.
[*]Beat them in order: Brock, Misty, Lt. Surge, Erika, Sabrina, Koga, Blaine and Clair, then the Elite Four in any order, then the Champion.
[*][b]Level cap[/b]: your first gym battle starts the challenge. Past your cap your Pokémon gain no battle experience, and a leader won't battle a team that is over it. It starts at 15 and rises with every win.
[*][b]Badges[/b]: each gym leader gives their badge the first time you win.
[*][b]Trainer Card[/b]: craft one to see your level cap, your wins and the trainers in order. Hold it and an arrow points to your next trainer once their gym has loaded.
[*][b]Rematches[/b]: the button under a gym's sign calls its leader back for one type gem.
[/list]

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]905 Pokémon[/b]: every species Cobblemon has, with their regional forms, gendered and shiny looks, cries and animations, spawning in the biomes and at the times of day Cobblemon gives them.
[*][b]Legendary Pokémon[/b]: 18 legendary and mythical Pokémon spawn in the wild, ultra rare, in biomes that fit them, some only by day, at night or in the right weather.
[*][b]Turn-based battles[/b]: Cobblemon's battle screen with its moves, abilities, stat stages, statuses, weather, held items and each move's animation, sounds and particles. Fight, switch, use items, catch or run.
[*][b]Party and PC[/b]: six Pokémon in their balls with the party overlay, a PC with 40 boxes of 30, and pastures where boxed Pokémon roam.
[*][b]Catching[/b]: all 49 Poké Balls with their own catch rules, and the throw, shake and capture of the mod.
[*][b]Evolution[/b]: by level, by the 52 evolution items and by trade, with Cobblemon's evolution animation.
[*][b]Training[/b]: natures, IVs and EVs, 335 TMs and the TM Machine, held items, friendship, candies and 168 marks.
[*][b]Healing[/b]: the Healing Machine puts your party's balls on its tray and heals the whole team.
[*][b]Riding[/b]: 93 species you can ride, 43 of them flying, with stamina and the ride controls on screen.
[*][b]Pokédex and scanner[/b]: register what you see and catch, and scan Pokémon in the world.
[*][b]Multiplayer[/b]: trade Pokémon with other players and challenge them to battles.
[*][b]Living world[/b]: wild Pokémon move in herds, flee when hurt, some fight back, and they sleep on Cobblemon's own schedule.
[*][b]Berries, apricorns, fossils and fishing[/b]: 70 berry bushes, seven colours of apricorn tree, fossils revived in a Restoration Tank, and Poké Rod fishing with 48 rods and bait.
[*][b]Cooking[/b]: the Campfire Pot with Cobblemon's 117 recipes, seasonings and Aprijuices.
[*][b]Structures[/b]: Cobblemon's ruins and other generated structures with their loot, plus the gyms with their furniture.
[/list]

[h2]Controls[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Send out or call back a Pokémon[/b]: use the Party item (hotbar slot 3)
[*][b]Pick the next Pokémon[/b]: sneak and use the Party item
[*][b]Battle a wild Pokémon[/b]: use the Party item on it, or use it with an empty hand
[*][b]Catch[/b]: in battle, choose Catch, then throw a Poké Ball at it
[*][b]Summary, held item, Ride, Shoulder, Stay[/b]: sneak and use one of your Pokémon for its wheel
[*][b]Heal[/b]: use a Potion on your Pokémon, or a Healing Machine for the whole party
[*][b]Ride[/b]: use a rideable Pokémon; double-tap forward to sprint, sneak to get off
[*][b]Fly[/b]: look where to go, hold jump to climb, look down while moving to dive
[*][b]Challenge a gym leader[/b]: step on the plate in the gym's doorway, then use the leader
[*][b]Find your next gym trainer[/b]: use the Trainer Card to read it, hold it for the arrow
[*][b]Pokédex[/b]: tap use to open it, hold use for the scanner
[*][b]Fish[/b]: use a Poké Rod to cast, and again when the bobber splashes
[*][b]Trade or battle a player[/b]: sneak and use the other player
[/list]
The README book in your hotbar lists every control.

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]The battle music is not in the download. Battles play without it.
[*]Bedrock add-ons cannot add new keys, so the Party item takes the place of Cobblemon's send-out and party keys.
[*]Every menu works with a controller: the D-pad or left stick moves between buttons, A presses and B closes. On a keyboard the arrow keys and Enter do the same.
[*]Battles are single battles, one Pokémon a side.
[*]The Trainer Card can only point to a gym trainer whose building has already been loaded, so explore to find them.
[*]A few Pokémon on the Elite Four's and the Champion's teams are left out where Cobblemon has no model for them yet.
[*]The port follows the mod closely and is still growing. The [url=https://github.com/kirbycope/cobblemon-bedrock#readme]README on GitHub[/url] lists what is carried over and what is not yet.
[/list]

[h2]Reporting issues[/h2]
Comments are off on this page. Report bugs on [url=https://github.com/kirbycope/cobblemon-bedrock/issues]GitHub Issues[/url]. Say which Pokémon, gym or item it was, what you did, and what happened, and add a screenshot or clip if you can.

